 @page swift_debugging Debugging Hints

# On-the-fly Validation

## Dependency Checks

When compiled in assert or debug mode, we insert automatic dependency checks to
verify on-the-fly that the expected task dependencies are indeed respected. For
more details, see Particle._add_dependency_checks() in
python/swift2/particle/Particle.py.

The dependency checks introduce a sizeable overhead and come at a significant
run time cost. They can be disabled by passing the
`-DNoParticleDependencyChecks` macro definition to the compiler. Alternately,
you can add that flag in the python project using
```
peano4_project.output.makefile.add_CXX_flag("-DNoParticleDependencyChecks")
```


## Assignment Checks

When compiled in assert or debug mode, we insert automatic particle-grid
assigmnet checks to verify on-the-fly that the expected particle-grid
assignments, movements, and exchanges are indeed respected. For more details,
see the documentation of toolbox::particles::assignmentchecks in
src/toolbox/particles/assignmentchecks/TracingAPI.h.

The dependency checks introduce a sizeable overhead and come at a significant
run time cost. They can be disabled by passing the `-DnoAssignmentChecks` macro
definition to the compiler. Alternately,
you can add that flag in the python project using
```
peano4_project.output.makefile.add_CXX_flag("-DNoAssignmentChecks")
```





 */

